A||||12||beer_stud_21||ABC show "Downtown" about street racing.||||1||
Z||000000||beer_stud_21||08-02-2001||05:00 AM||||Did anyone else see that show "Downtown" with the segment on street racing?   I was suprised to see the guy they followed in the story wasn't a ricer driver.  He was some computer techie that had a 90k Pontiac TA that he said would do 190.  Showed him going to these huge race gathering things where he would go to find races.  He raced and beat a Supra on the highway.  They were goin something like 130 and had to shut it down when cars showed up in front of them.  The sad part of it is this guy is making bank with his techie job but is totally broke because of all the money he spends on his cars.  Has his family shacked up in some 2 bedroom apartment and leaves his pregnant wife at home when he goes out racing at night.  Said he even races people when she is in the car.  So anyone else see this show and want to comment?<P>-Marlin||||reg||1
Z||000001||TRiAD||08-02-2001||10:13 AM||||Didn't see it, but the guy sounds like a loser. He could be providing them a good life instead of just risking it. ||||reg||1
Z||000002||MinnGreenGT||08-02-2001||11:34 AM||||Yeah, I saw that last night! That guy was such a dumbass!  He said that he spent about $90K on his TA... with an ugly orange vinyl "Bird" on the hood.  I have trouble believing that he has had the car up to 190... but hey, for 90 grand you better be able to. As for his wife- she needs to move on! My wife said that if I ever acted and spent money like that, she'd leave me!  Anyway, I think the guy was a moron- if he's so sure his car will kick-butt all night, why doesn't he head down to the local Drag track and get some real timeslips- instead of endangering his pregnant wife and others on the street!  Don't take this wrong, I'm not anti-street racing... but you've still gotta use your brain!<P>------------------<BR>________________________<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/grngt.jpg">  <P>Medium Metallic Green 87 GT<BR>3.1L High Output<BR>4 Spd OD Tranny<BR>Open (read Loud) Exhaust<BR>and More!<p>[This message has been edited by MinnGreenGT (edited 08-02-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000003||MinnGreenGT||08-02-2001||11:46 AM||||I just looked it up... for those interested, check this out:<P><A HREF="http://abcnews.go.com/sections/Downtown/2020/Downtown_010801_streetracing.html" TARGET=_blank>http://abcnews.go.com/sections/Downtown/2020/Downtown_010801_streetracing.html</A><P>-Rob||||reg||1
Z||000004||Black88GT||08-02-2001||12:08 PM||||Yeah I saw it too, that guy is a moron.  Kinda reminds me of this A&E special about street racing in Toronto.  They had some 23 year old I am stuck in H.S. loser with a Civic HB that ran like 11s or 12s all motor, he lived with his mom, and said he spent 60 grand on his Civic.  Some people....||||reg||10
Z||000005||fierobaby||08-02-2001||12:57 PM||||that man on downtown really made me mad... he has a wife his wifes child from another marrige and a baby on the way and he was complaining about how much the baby cost himif ym husband did that he would be gone so quickly that man makes so much in his job he could give his family a huge house with a big yard for his kids and a puppy... nice clothes and food but instead he spends it on some ugly car!||||reg||1
Z||000006||b lo 0||08-02-2001||01:36 PM||||I saw it-what a loser!  The guy looked like that was how he considers his self-worth.  I personally don't like street racing, sure, I'll give a go with the Civic next to me, but nowhere over 70-80 mph on public roads.  If you look in an issue of Super Street (import mag) they always mention their "Keep It Off the Streets" policy, which is their personal battle against street racing.  They even have pictures in the back of imports that have been wrecked racing.  The story really hit home with me, here in Atlanta we've had 4 kids die street racing just in the last year.  Pretty sad.  Good segment tho.  I go to street shows sometimes (nothing else to do in Snellville) but I never race.  Be safe guys!<P>------------------<BR><FONT SIZE="1">'85 GT (in progress)<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.angelfire.com/ga3/audioimagery/ice.gif">      <BR>White Lightnin!  (NOT moonshine, for all you hillbillies!)</FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000007||DRH||08-02-2001||01:44 PM||||I'm not sure who's more of an idiot... Him, or her for staying with him. She made one statement about she couldn't count how many times she had gotten out of the car crying after he raced with her in there. <B>Quit getting in the car!!!</B> Must be some variation of a battered wife that won't leave. Then again, he probably has a nice life insurance policy... Maybe she's just waiting for that late night call from the cops???<P>What got me was the one scene where there was barely enough room for the cars to get through because of all the spectators standing <B>in the street</B>.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/eek.gif"><P><BR><p>[This message has been edited by DRH (edited 08-02-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000008||ferg||08-02-2001||01:56 PM||||I didn't see the show, but I found this thread in the GP-Owners forum, which I just became a member of.<P>The guy featured on the story is also a member of that forum and also a member of LS1.com. In this thread, you can read his responses to the story.<BR> <A HREF="http://www.gp-owners.com/forum/topic.asp?TOPIC_ID=6367971&FORUM_ID=1&CAT_ID=1&Topic_Title=Grand+Prix+on+20%2F20+Downtown%3F&Forum_Title=ClubGP+%2D+General" TARGET=_blank>http://www.gp-owners .com/forum/topic.asp?TOPIC_ID=6367971&FORUM_ID=1&CAT_ID=1&Topic_Title=Grand+Prix+on+20%2F20+Downtown%3F&Forum_Title=ClubGP+%2D+General</A> <P>I'm not going to choose a side, just thought it's interesting to read comments from the person featured in the show.<p>[This message has been edited by ferg (edited 08-02-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000009||JSocha||08-02-2001||02:09 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by DRH:<BR><B>I'm not sure who's more of an idiot... Him, or her for staying with him. She made one statement about she couldn't count how many times she had gotten out of the car crying after he raced with her in there. [b]Quit getting in the car!!!</B> Must be some variation of a battered wife that won't leave. Then again, he probably has a nice life insurance policy... Maybe she's just waiting for that late night call from the cops???[/B]<HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>&lt;pun intended&gt; Maybe she's just along for the ride.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/jsocha_2.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000010||thomas_l||08-03-2001||09:58 AM||||Street racing is not news. When I was just out of high school I did the cruising and street racing thing too - I just wasn't able to fund the "king racer" car with my crappy pay at the time. The closest I got (don't laff  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">) was the (new at the time) 83 Mustang GT. Bone stock because the car payment and insurance ate up any extra cash I managed to earn.<P>The only thing that bugged me about the clip was the racing with the wife/kid in the car - pretty stupid. I think the only reason he street races is that is the only venue he can be a "winner" every time, considering the bucks he dumps into that T/A and the usual poor teenagers he is challenging. He doesn't have the balls for sanctioned racing because most of the people there are better drivers and have better cars.<P>As far as the money he spends, that's his choice on priorities. If he was cruising in a $80K S500 nobody would have $hit to say. Likewise if that T/A was loaded on a trailer behind a new Navigator headed to the drag strip. Everyone has their hobby, some can afford to spend more on theirs. That show was so typical. They put a really big spin on all the bad stuff and it was real obvious. Just a lame ploy off of "Fast and Furious" to sell ad revenue. If ABC had done a special on NHRA or SCCA (where people freely pour more money than sense into their hobbies) nobody would watch it.||||reg||1
Z||000011||Formula||08-03-2001||03:48 PM||||he has a $500K house too..... they didnt mention that.  He has 4 cars that require $2500 a month in insurance, gas, repairs, etc.... he said he only has a about $10k in his T/A,  For some reason the story doesnt seem like they told the whole truth.||||reg||1
